  "Number": 11,
  "Question": "The angles of quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) satisfy \\(\\angle A=2\\angle B=3\\angle C=4\\angle D.\\) What is the degree measure of \\(\\angle A,\\) rounded to the nearest whole number?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(125\\)",
    "B": "\\(144\\)",
    "C": "\\(153\\)",
    "D": "\\(173\\)",
    "E": "\\(180\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The given chain expresses the other angles in terms of \\(\\angle A\\): they are one-half, one-third, and one-fourth of it. Multiplying these relative amounts by \\(12\\) gives\n\\[\n\\angle A:\\angle B:\\angle C:\\angle D\n=12:6:4:3.\n\\]\nA quadrilateral has interior angle sum \\(360^\\circ\\). There are \\(12+6+4+3=25\\) equal shares in the ratio, and \\(\\angle A\\) receives \\(12\\) of them. Hence\n\\[\n\\angle A=\\frac{12}{25}\\cdot360^\\circ=172.8^\\circ.\n\\]\nThe tenths digit is \\(8\\), so rounding to the nearest whole degree gives \\(173^\\circ\\), choice D.",
